gradle-wrapper.jar
/.gradle
/captures/
/gradlew
/gradlew.bat
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# ONE EXCEPTION, AND IT IS NOT A KEYSTORE WORTH HIDING.
#
# demo/demo.keystore signs the demo APK only. Its password is `android`, it can never reach the
# Play Store, and anybody can generate an equivalent in ten seconds — so the rule above protects
# nothing here while costing something real: without a FIXED key, every demo build is signed by a
# different one, Android refuses to install it over the previous version, and the only way through
# is to uninstall and lose everything the app remembered. That happened to the founder on
# 2026-08-10 and is the reason this line exists.
#
# The upload key is still covered by the rule above and still never enters the tree.
!demo/demo.keystore
